WEBVTT

00:08.690 --> 00:11.030
Just like I thought.

00:11.530 --> 00:12.070
What is?

00:12.400 --> 00:15.660
You're someone who will cherish me.

00:16.240 --> 00:17.330
What's that?

00:17.580 --> 00:22.120
I don't want to have anything to do with someone who won't cherish me.

00:22.120 --> 00:25.920
If that's the case, I'd rather be alone.

00:26.210 --> 00:27.210
Miyako...

00:27.210 --> 00:30.460
I don't want to disappear from someone's heart again.

00:30.460 --> 00:33.550
If it's like that, I'd rather we had never met.

00:40.310 --> 00:43.310
Can I stay here?

00:43.690 --> 00:44.390
Yeah.

00:44.730 --> 00:47.860
Can you look at me alone at all times?

00:48.190 --> 00:48.900
Yeah.

00:48.900 --> 00:52.900
I don't want to let go of something important to me anymore.

00:58.660 --> 01:01.500
Fly high, make it

01:01.500 --> 01:04.750
Get to the new world that I seek

01:05.000 --> 01:11.380
Someday with my little wings

01:11.380 --> 01:17.550
Don't look back to the sorrow I left behind

01:17.760 --> 01:23.770
Here's my real intention I hide

01:24.310 --> 01:30.480
I wish you were here, and so just right by my side

01:30.730 --> 01:36.820
Need to be strong enough to swallow my pride

01:37.070 --> 01:42.790
I have been looking for my own style

01:42.790 --> 01:50.290
Don't give it up, here comes the life

01:53.170 --> 01:55.920
Be alive, take it

01:55.920 --> 01:59.180
Promise to find, yes I will

01:59.470 --> 02:05.640
Shining wings filled with wishes

02:05.980 --> 02:08.730
Fly high, make it

02:08.730 --> 02:12.190
Get to the new world that I seek

02:12.230 --> 02:18.700
Someday, so I believe

02:42.350 --> 02:43.600
What's this about?

02:44.260 --> 02:45.430
Kei...

02:45.430 --> 02:46.890
Is this what it's about?

02:48.810 --> 02:50.020
Your...

03:04.030 --> 03:04.700
Kei!

03:12.580 --> 03:13.710
Don't go.

03:20.930 --> 03:21.800
Miyako...

03:22.140 --> 03:24.430
Don't go, please.

03:24.810 --> 03:25.430
But...

03:25.720 --> 03:27.430
Who do you choose, her or me?

03:28.430 --> 03:30.190
You're not going, are you, Hirono-kun?

03:32.350 --> 03:35.400
Look at me alone. Don't look at anyone other than me!

03:35.860 --> 03:36.730
Miyako...

03:37.190 --> 03:38.240
Please.

03:48.620 --> 03:50.870
Wait here. I'll be back real soon.

03:54.580 --> 03:57.090
You left after all.

04:03.890 --> 04:04.760
Kei-chan...

04:06.930 --> 04:07.850
Don't worry about me!

04:10.100 --> 04:11.480
Don't you want to shoot this?

04:12.770 --> 04:15.400
You want to shoot this, right? Shoot it!

04:17.190 --> 04:21.400
Just shoot it. Such an amusing scene won't happen a second time.

04:21.400 --> 04:22.740
Shoot it!

04:23.280 --> 04:24.160
Kei-chan...

04:41.670 --> 04:42.470
Kei...

04:42.880 --> 04:44.130
Incoming Call

04:42.880 --> 04:44.130
Tsutsumi Kyosuke

04:44.760 --> 04:45.390
It's me.

04:45.680 --> 04:47.720
Sorry, I'm busy right now.

04:47.720 --> 04:49.010
Because of Kei-chan?

04:50.140 --> 04:51.520
Can we meet?

04:54.850 --> 04:56.350
What do you want all of a sudden?

04:56.350 --> 04:58.360
I'm the one who should be asking you that.

04:58.610 --> 05:00.360
What are you planning to do, Hirono?

05:00.650 --> 05:02.070
Planning to do...?

05:02.990 --> 05:05.740
Are you going out with Miyamura?

05:05.740 --> 05:07.700
How is that relevant?

05:08.120 --> 05:09.950
What about Kei-chan then?

05:10.410 --> 05:14.210
What are you saying? Kei and I don't have that kind of relationship...

05:15.250 --> 05:16.750
What the heck is this about?

05:16.750 --> 05:19.290
You're leaving things half done.

05:19.290 --> 05:22.340
You're half-assed about your studies, about your work.

05:22.340 --> 05:24.930
Don't abuse others like that!

05:24.930 --> 05:26.590
Stop saying things I don't understand!

05:27.720 --> 05:30.390
Do you think you can beat me with your left hand?

05:30.390 --> 05:31.890
My right hand is for work!

05:32.270 --> 05:33.640
You're half-assed even at fighting.

05:33.640 --> 05:34.600
What?

05:34.940 --> 05:36.940
You try to run away from everything like that, don't you?

05:36.940 --> 05:38.520
I've never tried to run away!

05:38.520 --> 05:42.030
Taking something on without thinking about it and then dragging it along

05:42.030 --> 05:43.860
is the same as running away!

05:45.110 --> 05:49.660
Didn't you run away without trying to persuade your dad too?

05:49.660 --> 05:52.200
What do you know about my family?

05:52.450 --> 05:53.830
What is Kei-chan to you?

05:55.000 --> 05:56.750
Is she family, or a woman?

05:56.750 --> 05:58.920
Neither. Kei is Kei.

05:59.170 --> 06:01.380
That's why I said you're half-assed!

06:01.380 --> 06:04.460
She cried because you didn't make yourself clear!

06:05.380 --> 06:09.890
You're making her suffer because you're running away with your indecisive attitude.

06:10.680 --> 06:17.140
At this rate, she'll follow you forever, crying like a lost child.

06:18.480 --> 06:22.650
You're the only one, Hirono, who can help her with her feelings.

06:26.650 --> 06:27.610
I'm back.

06:28.910 --> 06:30.070
Miyako?

06:39.330 --> 06:40.250
Miyako...

06:43.500 --> 06:44.630
Hirono-kun?

06:44.630 --> 06:45.670
Miyako...?

06:45.670 --> 06:47.300
I've thought about it.

06:47.300 --> 06:48.130
About what?

06:48.130 --> 06:50.510
Let's not see each other anymore.

06:50.970 --> 06:52.600
What are you saying, Miyako?

06:53.220 --> 06:57.390
It's painful for me to think about you.

06:58.440 --> 07:02.770
I know I'm saying something selfish. I also know it's wrong for me to do this.

07:02.770 --> 07:07.940
But your heart doesn't belong to me and me alone after all.

07:08.650 --> 07:09.780
Miyako...

07:09.780 --> 07:15.990
One day, I'll disappear from your heart again when it fills with other things, right?

07:16.580 --> 07:19.960
Therefore, let's break up before that happens.

07:19.960 --> 07:22.710
Wait, Miyako! Miyako!

07:24.000 --> 07:25.670
Incoming Mail History

07:24.000 --> 07:25.670
Public Telephone

07:24.000 --> 07:25.670
Tsutsumi
Kyosuke

07:32.140 --> 07:33.010
Miyako...

07:42.440 --> 07:43.560
Hiro-senpai.

07:44.940 --> 07:45.770
Hayama.

07:46.610 --> 07:48.820
What are you doing here?

07:49.110 --> 07:50.320
Nothing.

07:50.860 --> 07:53.240
How was Kei-senpai's sandwich?

07:53.240 --> 07:53.870
Eh?

07:53.870 --> 07:57.700
She suddenly called me up last night and asked me how to make it.

07:57.700 --> 07:58.870
How frustrating.

07:58.870 --> 07:59.580
O-O-Ouch.

07:59.580 --> 08:01.500
Wh-What on earth is that about?

08:01.500 --> 08:05.790
She suddenly began to cook. I thought it was strange, so I asked her.

08:05.790 --> 08:10.840
And she said boldly, "It's for Onii-chan".

08:10.840 --> 08:12.840
Plus her face was all red.

08:12.840 --> 08:18.520
I had no choice, so I taught her how to make it while holding back my tears for her happiness.

08:18.520 --> 08:20.270
I-I see.

08:20.270 --> 08:23.810
Well, I got something in return.

08:23.810 --> 08:24.770
What's that?

08:24.770 --> 08:27.270
Tokyo Metropolitan Area Suginami Ward Igusa
Post Office PO Box No. A T 9

08:24.770 --> 08:27.270
Monthly Publication
Manager of Surveys

08:24.770 --> 08:27.270
Paste ID and Code

08:24.770 --> 08:27.270
Third Choice

08:25.230 --> 08:27.270
The subscription postcard to the monthly publication MIMI.

08:27.520 --> 08:31.110
This month's present to the reader is extremely valuable.

08:32.070 --> 08:33.820
What are you doing?

08:33.820 --> 08:36.450
Hayama, are you a fan of Shindou Nagi?

08:34.360 --> 08:36.450
Monthly

08:34.360 --> 08:36.450
Publication

08:34.360 --> 08:36.450
Reader Survey

08:34.360 --> 08:36.450
Circle 3 works that you found interesting, and put a cross on

08:34.360 --> 08:36.450
Shindou Nagi

08:34.360 --> 08:36.450
Name of the author (original author) whom you like

08:34.360 --> 08:36.450
all the works you didn't read

08:34.360 --> 08:36.450
Blue Sky

08:34.360 --> 08:36.450
Melody

08:34.360 --> 08:36.450
Witch Kiss

08:34.360 --> 08:36.450
Sky of Time

08:34.360 --> 08:36.450
Toomiya's Town

08:34.360 --> 08:36.450
Magic Ninja

08:34.360 --> 08:36.450
Welcome

08:34.360 --> 08:36.450
Honey Romance

08:34.360 --> 08:36.450
Last Room

08:34.360 --> 08:36.450
Azeta

08:34.360 --> 08:36.450
Angel Note

08:34.360 --> 08:36.450
Your time

08:36.450 --> 08:39.370
Yeah, since his name is similar to Kei-senpai's.

08:39.370 --> 08:40.870
That's it?

08:42.660 --> 08:46.790
Eh? It's a different author for "works of interest"?

08:46.790 --> 08:50.800
Because lately, Shindou Nagi's works haven't been interesting.

08:51.840 --> 08:57.600
Somehow his vigor has decreased. His works used to have more sparkle to them.

08:58.100 --> 09:02.850
Lately, his works have been too ordinary. They're not Shindou Nagi-like anymore.

09:03.350 --> 09:06.310
Even though you wouldn't understand that.

09:06.600 --> 09:08.110
Y-Yeah.

09:11.400 --> 09:14.320
Being half-assed at everything... huh?

09:16.530 --> 09:18.450
I know that.

09:28.960 --> 09:32.300
Knowing something and understanding it are different.

09:32.960 --> 09:34.720
I know that too.

09:36.970 --> 09:41.180
They're all important to you, so you don't want to let go of any of them, right?

09:41.180 --> 09:43.220
Yeah, something like that.

09:43.220 --> 09:46.310
But one day you'll have to give up on one of them.

09:47.310 --> 09:50.230
For the sake of not letting go of what's most important to you.

09:50.230 --> 09:52.860
As I said, they're all important to me.

09:52.860 --> 09:56.450
But if you don't choose one, you'll end up losing everything.

09:56.450 --> 10:01.200
Even so, I can't abandon something I got involved with and pretend nothing happened.

10:01.200 --> 10:03.240
You're not abandoning it.

10:08.170 --> 10:10.250
They're asking you to abandon it.

10:12.550 --> 10:14.260
That's why it's painful.

10:16.420 --> 10:19.470
I don't want to get hurt anymore.

10:20.050 --> 10:23.770
But as long as you live, you can't run away from pain.

10:25.770 --> 10:29.150
I know. I know that, but...

10:29.560 --> 10:34.860
Letting go of a bond that you created will cause you the same pain as having your body torn apart.

10:37.320 --> 10:39.610
Can you guys bear it?

10:39.610 --> 10:42.660
We shouldn't run away even if we can't bear it.

10:44.410 --> 10:45.500
You're right.

10:47.330 --> 10:50.210
Career Interest Survey; Submission Dead line April 27th

10:52.960 --> 10:56.340
You actually knew the answer from the very beginning, didn't you?

10:56.920 --> 11:01.220
Even if I did, I lacked the courage to understand its meaning.

11:04.140 --> 11:09.690
I feel like... I've seen the color I've been looking for.

11:25.950 --> 11:27.620
Kei, are you there?

11:29.120 --> 11:30.670
What are you doing here?

11:31.170 --> 11:32.920
You forgot your crutch.

11:32.920 --> 11:33.960
Go home.

11:33.960 --> 11:36.090
Don't push yourself before your knee recovers.

11:36.090 --> 11:37.510
It's none of your business.

11:37.960 --> 11:41.300
Kei, thank you for the sandwiches.

11:44.890 --> 11:46.890
I ran into Hayama and heard about it from her.

11:46.890 --> 11:50.390
And she told me that my manga wasn't interesting.

11:51.980 --> 11:56.820
Kei, I'm going to quit school and devote myself to being a manga artist.

11:57.900 --> 12:01.450
It wasn't right to do an indifferent job on it till now.

12:01.450 --> 12:05.280
I can't draw something well if I'm indecisive about it.

12:05.780 --> 12:09.290
Is that related to Miyamura-senpai?

12:09.290 --> 12:12.540
It's not unrelated, but it's something I thought through myself.

12:12.870 --> 12:14.250
You've decided?

12:14.250 --> 12:15.290
Yeah, I've decided.

12:15.630 --> 12:19.550
I see. You were always like that.

12:21.130 --> 12:24.720
You decide everything on your own and proceed ahead by yourself.

12:25.970 --> 12:26.800
Kei...

12:26.800 --> 12:29.930
You fulfill your dream and do what you want to do.

12:29.930 --> 12:33.390
You carry it through to the end, even though it's hard.

12:33.390 --> 12:34.690
Because you've been watching out for me.

12:35.060 --> 12:35.690
Eh?

12:36.020 --> 12:39.860
I wanted to act cool in front of the girls who called me "Onii-chan".

12:40.190 --> 12:44.700
I wanted to make you two happy. That's why I started drawing manga.

12:45.030 --> 12:46.160
Onii-chan...

12:50.450 --> 12:52.910
It was fun back then.

12:52.910 --> 12:55.960
Do you remember? We fought while we were reading this manga.

12:55.960 --> 12:56.580
Yeah.

12:58.090 --> 12:59.920
What was that about?

12:59.920 --> 13:03.170
The last chapter took an unexpected turn. We were surprised.

13:03.800 --> 13:08.430
The three of us, including Chihiro, argued about whether we liked or hated the way it ended.

13:09.010 --> 13:13.020
You took the side of the girl who got dumped at the very end.

13:13.390 --> 13:16.980
You insisted it was her fault that she got dumped.

13:16.980 --> 13:21.530
She didn't make any effort, just because she was kind of pretty.

13:22.070 --> 13:25.030
Now that I think about it, that was already the end.

13:25.700 --> 13:29.870
But we didn't even realize it and were absorbed in the ending.

13:30.410 --> 13:33.330
That's what reality is.

13:33.330 --> 13:34.410
Yeah.

13:34.870 --> 13:37.130
It's impossible to have a fair ending.

13:37.420 --> 13:39.420
That ending was more realistic.

13:40.090 --> 13:43.840
One day, it suddenly comes to an end without prior notice.

13:44.340 --> 13:50.050
The one who's been dreaming about it before like an idiot is destroyed in an instant.

13:50.720 --> 13:51.260
Kei...

13:51.260 --> 13:52.140
Don't say it!

13:53.600 --> 13:55.600
Don't end it yet.

13:56.480 --> 13:57.310
Kei...

13:57.600 --> 14:02.320
I thought our relationship would continue forever and ever.

14:02.320 --> 14:04.820
You'd be with me, I'd be with you.

14:04.820 --> 14:08.870
You'd always be sloppy and need me to take care of you.

14:09.490 --> 14:15.710
But I'd always do my best to support you, and you'd support me when I was having a hard time.

14:16.120 --> 14:19.000
We'd fight sometimes, then make up.

14:19.000 --> 14:22.750
Eventually, our relationship as brother and sister would turn into being lovers.

14:22.750 --> 14:26.760
Before long, we'd get married and have kids.

14:26.760 --> 14:31.350
It would... It would keep going on like that.

14:32.390 --> 14:33.100
Kei...

14:33.930 --> 14:37.810
What did you think, Onii-chan? Tell me the truth.

14:38.350 --> 14:44.360
I thought something like that as well. I thought it would somehow turn out that way.

14:44.360 --> 14:51.030
Really? So it was just too late for me to find out.

14:51.530 --> 14:54.700
I should've admitted my feelings sooner.

14:55.290 --> 14:57.370
Sorry, Kei.

14:59.080 --> 15:00.920
Onii-chan, I love you!

15:02.130 --> 15:03.250
I love you.

15:03.590 --> 15:07.590
I love you, Onii-chan.

15:08.220 --> 15:08.930
Yeah.

15:09.260 --> 15:11.890
All this time, since we were small.

15:12.390 --> 15:13.010
Yeah.

15:13.390 --> 15:15.390
I yearned for it.

15:15.390 --> 15:15.890
Yeah.

15:16.140 --> 15:18.140
It was my pride.

15:18.140 --> 15:18.940
Yeah.

15:18.940 --> 15:22.150
I had... I had always loved you.

15:22.150 --> 15:22.730
Yeah.

15:28.860 --> 15:33.530
I want to go back. To the time when we were always together.

15:34.160 --> 15:36.790
To the time when you were with me.

15:37.580 --> 15:38.540
We can.

15:39.830 --> 15:41.290
Let's go back, Kei.

15:41.290 --> 15:44.210
Even though we're not related by blood, you're my younger sister.

15:44.210 --> 15:46.380
You're someone important to me.

15:46.380 --> 15:46.960
That's why...

15:50.760 --> 15:54.970
What... It was painful for you too.

15:57.390 --> 15:58.720
I see.

15:59.060 --> 15:59.810
Kei...

16:00.640 --> 16:02.940
I'll be all right.

16:02.940 --> 16:06.900
I think it'll take some time, but I'll definitely be all right.

16:08.280 --> 16:08.820
Okay.

16:13.110 --> 16:15.030
This is my last time looking at this place too, eh.

16:15.910 --> 16:17.330
Are you running away again?

16:17.580 --> 16:19.830
It's the same as before anyway.

16:19.830 --> 16:22.040
I just need to turn a blind eye to what I don't like.

16:22.040 --> 16:24.750
I just need to stop my ears against what I don't want to hear.

16:24.750 --> 16:27.210
I've always done that, and I've survived until now that way.

16:27.500 --> 16:29.630
You won't be able to choose anything then.

16:29.630 --> 16:32.880
It's fine. I gave up on that from the very beginning.

16:33.220 --> 16:35.800
But that person is trying his best.

16:35.800 --> 16:39.640
I can't be as strong as Hirono-kun.

16:39.640 --> 16:42.520
That's a pity. I wanted to watch it.

16:43.270 --> 16:46.980
A dream that might bring someone like me happiness.

16:49.400 --> 16:50.440
A dream?

16:59.870 --> 17:01.000
Is this Miyako?

17:01.000 --> 17:02.000
Yeah.

17:02.000 --> 17:02.960
Where are you now?

17:02.960 --> 17:03.830
That's a secret.

17:03.830 --> 17:05.370
Can we talk face to face?

17:05.370 --> 17:07.670
No. My determination will waver if we meet.

17:07.670 --> 17:08.920
Determination means...

17:08.920 --> 17:11.130
I'm going to leave this town.

17:11.130 --> 17:13.340
And then I'm going to a place nobody knows.

17:13.720 --> 17:15.180
Miyako...

17:15.180 --> 17:17.300
This is my last call.

17:17.300 --> 17:20.850
This is my last farewell to you, who has been nice to me.

17:20.850 --> 17:21.850
Miyako...

17:22.180 --> 17:26.520
I think I might've been testing you till now.

17:26.520 --> 17:27.520
Testing means...?

17:27.520 --> 17:30.360
Ever since we met on Christmas night...

17:30.730 --> 17:34.030
I think I've been observing your reactions since then.

17:34.030 --> 17:37.870
To see if you were someone who'd cherish me.

17:38.120 --> 17:40.700
You didn't need to go as far as testing me for something like that...

17:40.700 --> 17:44.540
If I wasn't going to be cherished, I didn't want to get involved with anyone.

17:44.960 --> 17:47.040
And then? How was it?

17:47.790 --> 17:50.210
The result of the testing. Did I fail?

17:50.210 --> 17:52.050
Nah. You got full marks.

17:52.050 --> 17:54.880
You're a nice person, and too good for me.

17:54.880 --> 17:56.300
Don't say that.

17:56.300 --> 17:58.720
I have an eye for people.

17:58.720 --> 18:01.220
Then why'd you say you're going to leave town?

18:01.220 --> 18:04.390
I don't want to be erased from your heart.

18:04.640 --> 18:07.230
I'm going to make myself disappear while you still love me.

18:07.230 --> 18:08.440
Miyako...

18:08.440 --> 18:11.190
There wasn't a sound in my house.

18:11.190 --> 18:11.900
Sound?

18:11.900 --> 18:14.740
My parents were always at work.

18:14.740 --> 18:17.570
Both papa and mama kept their mouths shut at home.

18:17.570 --> 18:23.240
They didn't talk at all. They didn't even want to hear each other's voices or footsteps.

18:23.240 --> 18:27.920
Their minds were full of hate for each other, and they were too busy to care about their own daughter.

18:27.920 --> 18:28.920
My name...

18:28.920 --> 18:29.920
Name?

18:29.920 --> 18:32.750
They hardly ever called my name.

18:33.170 --> 18:35.340
That's how little talking there was.

18:35.340 --> 18:40.260
No matter how well I did in school, even if I was number one in sports, they never praised me.

18:40.260 --> 18:44.100
I even learned how to prepare the fish recipe that papa and mama loved.

18:44.100 --> 18:46.930
I cut myself a lot with the kitchen knife, but...

18:47.600 --> 18:48.770
Miyako...

18:48.770 --> 18:55.440
It was strange though. I didn't really need to mimic them, but I always felt breathless anxiety.

18:55.440 --> 19:00.110
Finally, they got divorced about six years ago. Frankly speaking, I felt relieved.

19:00.110 --> 19:02.950
Because of that, I was free.

19:02.950 --> 19:08.620
After that, I quit that house without sound, and started going wherever I wanted to go freely.

19:08.620 --> 19:12.460
I hoped that I'd find a home somewhere one day.

19:13.750 --> 19:16.670
It was relaxing not to be involved with anyone.

19:16.670 --> 19:20.970
I didn't feel tired, and I didn't need to be careful to avoid being hated.

19:20.970 --> 19:23.800
I could go anywhere, whenever I liked.

19:24.470 --> 19:27.730
Yeah, I could go anywhere.

19:29.480 --> 19:35.730
But... But, being able to go anywhere meant that I didn't have a home anywhere.

19:35.730 --> 19:40.820
Not having a place I wanted to go to or return to was like being all alone in the world.

19:41.160 --> 19:42.200
Shut up!

19:42.990 --> 19:45.490
Stop babbling by yourself!

19:45.490 --> 19:46.490
Hirono-kun...

19:47.040 --> 19:50.540
Besides, why didn't you tell me about this sooner?

19:50.540 --> 19:52.920
You felt lonely, didn't you? You felt pain, didn't you?

19:52.920 --> 19:55.000
If so, you should've told me!

19:55.000 --> 19:58.840
There's no way I could tell you! If I had told you, you'd have pitied me.

19:58.840 --> 20:02.510
I wanted to be cherished, not pitied!

20:02.840 --> 20:05.350
In that case, your home will be by my side!

20:06.350 --> 20:11.020
In that case, your family and your life by yourself will become your past. It'll be okay then, right?

20:11.390 --> 20:14.440
Even if I have a home, I'll be afraid of losing it!

20:14.440 --> 20:15.610
You won't!

20:15.610 --> 20:17.690
How can you be so sure?

20:17.690 --> 20:18.820
Trust me.

20:18.820 --> 20:21.070
I want to. I want to trust you.

20:21.070 --> 20:22.360
Is there something you're not satisfied with?

20:22.360 --> 20:26.580
Because I'm horrible! You'll definitely hate me one day.

20:26.580 --> 20:28.040
That's not true!

20:28.040 --> 20:31.410
I knew how you and Kei-chan felt!

20:31.410 --> 20:33.710
I thought I couldn't win against Kei-chan.

20:33.710 --> 20:38.840
But I wanted to stay by your side so desperately that I held onto you.

20:38.840 --> 20:41.550
And I knew you were suffering!

20:41.550 --> 20:46.050
I'm the worst. I only think about myself!

20:46.050 --> 20:49.520
Let me think about my problems. You're just fine as you are.

20:49.520 --> 20:51.730
That's more like you.

20:53.230 --> 20:55.270
I've found the answer to my problem.

20:55.270 --> 20:56.400
The rest is up to you!

20:56.980 --> 20:59.230
Can I really trust you?

20:59.610 --> 21:00.230
Yeah.

21:00.610 --> 21:03.070
I don't want to disappear anymore.

21:03.070 --> 21:05.910
I'm right here, so I don't want to be ignored!

21:06.200 --> 21:08.740
I'm always looking at you. How could you disappear?!

21:08.740 --> 21:10.580
I want to stay!

21:10.580 --> 21:14.420
I want my cooking to be eaten while it's still warm!

21:14.750 --> 21:16.250
I want to be with you!

21:16.710 --> 21:20.090
I want someone to praise me!

21:20.090 --> 21:22.470
I'll say you're amazing if you do well in school!

21:22.470 --> 21:24.220
I'll scold you if you do something bad!

21:24.220 --> 21:25.760
And of course, I'll eat your cooking!

21:26.470 --> 21:30.010
No matter how disgraceful it is, I want to cling to you!

21:30.010 --> 21:33.270
You can just do what you want to do! I'll accept it all!

21:33.270 --> 21:35.190
Hirono-kun, I...

21:35.190 --> 21:38.940
Listen carefully! I...

22:22.400 --> 22:24.900
I... love you!

22:29.740 --> 22:30.740
Hirono-kun!

22:31.030 --> 22:32.700
I didn't know this place.

22:33.200 --> 22:35.660
I've gone to all the public telephones in Otowa.

22:36.000 --> 22:37.160
Hirono-kun.

22:37.500 --> 22:38.500
Miyako.

23:01.110 --> 23:02.860
You have to bear the responsibility.

23:02.860 --> 23:03.900
Responsibility?

23:03.900 --> 23:06.320
You caught me, so don't let me go anymore.

23:06.780 --> 23:09.320
You didn't want to be bound by anyone, did you?

23:09.610 --> 23:12.120
Human feelings can change.

23:41.310 --> 23:48.820
kawaranai mainichi meguri meguru

23:41.310 --> 23:48.820
Every day that comes around is unchanging

23:50.910 --> 23:57.240
nani mo nai jikan ga sugiru

23:50.910 --> 23:57.240
There’s nothing that goes around the passing time

24:00.580 --> 24:08.090
kaze ni yurameite arukidaseba

24:00.580 --> 24:08.090
The wind shakes as I’m beginning to walk

24:10.130 --> 24:18.600
itsuka kawaru ka na? ashita

24:10.130 --> 24:18.600
I wonder if it will change someday? Tomorrow

24:21.560 --> 24:30.990
nakushita mono wo sagashite wa akiramete

24:21.560 --> 24:30.990
I gave up searching for the thing I lost

24:31.150 --> 24:43.460
hitori tatazumi sora wo miteita

24:31.150 --> 24:43.460
Alone I stood still, as I was looking at the sky

24:46.630 --> 24:55.470
The girl is the only one in the world

24:56.260 --> 24:59.600
Carve me into the memories that won't disappear.

25:00.390 --> 25:03.810
Next episode, ef - a tale of memories:

25:04.140 --> 25:05.480
Ever forever.

25:06.230 --> 25:09.070
Do you have memories you don't want to forget?
